# gate-proofs.allow -- three namespaces for the gate-registry meta-gate.
#
# Bare lines: preflight slugs with neither a test suite naming their script nor a
# mutations.json entry. Baseline frozen 2026-09-03 at 15 of 33 slugs; 0 of 36
# today (the gate prints the live count every run -- read it there, not here). Three left on 2026-09-04 (doc-dupes, stdout-returns, pkg-names) and
# dockerfile-lint with them; the 2026-09-05 wave closed nine more --
# copy-coverage, patch-integrity, arg-consistency, mirror-consistency,
# runtime-paths, workflow-lint, secret-scan, android-parity, sbom -- each with a
# characterisation suite over the real gate plus mutations on its own script.
# The last two left on 2026-09-05 and this namespace is now EMPTY, which is the
# state it was built to reach. critical-fixes took the split its reason named:
# the /opt-probing half is 06-packaging/smoke-critical-fixes.sh, so what preflight
# runs reads the repo tree only. version-snapshot got the one-fixture-per-sub-check
# suite its reason demanded -- six of seven sub-checks plus the licence subprocess
# reddened independently, and the seventh pinned as a KNOWN GAP: its glob
# (windows/scripts/build-*-from-source.ps1) matches nothing, the scripts being one
# directory deeper, so it prints green over an empty file list. Both stories are in
# docs/code-quality-tooling.md#the-two-that-stay-frozen-with-better-reasons.
# An empty namespace is not a finished one: the next NEW slug lands here.
# The list only ratchets DOWN -- a NEW unproven slug fails gate-registry, and a
# line that has gained a proof is STALE and must be deleted. The cheapest
# proof per slug is sketched in docs/code-quality-tooling.md.
#
# mutation-id: lines: ids whose prefix names a preflight slug that does not own
# the target, or names no slug while pinning some gate's own file. Ratchets down
# the same way: rename the id in mutations.json and delete the line together.
# Empty since 2026-09-04: the registry now credits a gate for the helper its .sh
# shells out to and for a mutation that pins its CALL SITE in a shared
# orchestrator or a git hook, which is what all five frozen ids were.
#
# mutation-family: lines: declared descriptive prefixes for mutations over
# ORDINARY build scripts, which no gate owns. Not debt -- a vocabulary. An
# undeclared prefix fails, and a family no id carries any more is STALE.
mutation-family:android-env
mutation-family:boot
mutation-family:chain-status
mutation-family:cross-build
mutation-family:version-forwarding
mutation-family:dead-code
mutation-family:delete-guard
mutation-family:disk-guard
mutation-family:doc-numbers
mutation-family:env-knob-default
mutation-family:flutter
mutation-family:gate-fixture
mutation-family:gst
mutation-family:guard-helpers
mutation-family:handoff
mutation-family:harvest
mutation-family:lib
mutation-family:llvm-target
mutation-family:pre-commit
mutation-family:preflight-slugs
mutation-family:package
mutation-family:packaging
mutation-family:probe
mutation-family:python
mutation-family:qairt
mutation-family:rust
mutation-family:sccache
mutation-family:tree-arch
mutation-family:vulkan
mutation-family:wheels
mutation-family:trailing-return
# ORT single source on Linux (owner rule 2026-09-23): the OpenCV/FFmpeg/gst onnx build gates and the runtime gate.
mutation-family:ort-chain
# Consumer CI venvs inside our images end on the chain ORT wheels (python_uv.sh uv_reconcile_chain_ort).
mutation-family:uv-chain-ort
# The ORT census (G1 runtime smoke, G6 consumer bundles): 06-packaging/check-ort-provenance.sh + its probe.
mutation-family:ort-census
# No build-host setting in a published image's ENV (2026-09-23): the Linux wrapper gate's check and the
# Windows Dockerfiles it protects. The static pass's ids sit under dockerfile-lint.image-env-*.
mutation-family:image-env

# Arrived 2026-09-08 with the mutation coverage for this batch's new hub entry
# points. Each names the subject its ids describe, over files no preflight slug
# owns: the consumer-facing lint aggregator (linux/scripts/run-lint-gates.sh and
# 01-core/gates.sh, whose ids sit in the existing `lib` family), the bash twin of
# Sync-SharedConfig.ps1 together with shared-assets.manifest, and the consumer
# inventory gate.
#
# `ci-image-ref` covered a PAIR until 2026-09-15 for one stated reason:
# lint-workflows.sh runs verify_ci_image_refs.py through "${_PY}" and the registry
# could only read a literal `python3`. It reads the interpreter variable now, so
# workflow-lint owns that file by name and its five ids carry that prefix. What is
# left in this family is the shell half, ci-image-ref.sh: consumers and workflows
# call it, no preflight slug does, and test-ci-image-ref.sh is its proof.
# Arrived 2026-09-15 with the six upstreamed consumer helpers. Both name files
# no preflight slug owns: 01-core/bind-mount-ownership.sh, whose proof is
# tests/test-bind-mount-ownership.sh, and the PowerShell-lint half of the
# reusable .github/workflows/python-ci-windows.yml, whose proof is
# tests/test-reusable-windows-lane.sh. (The batch's other ids joined existing
# families: `lib` for cmake-build.sh, `packaging` for app-packaging.sh and
# `python` for the static-analysis driver.)
mutation-family:bind-mount
mutation-family:windows-lane
# 2026-09-24: its Linux twin, the `arches` plan step of the reusable
# .github/workflows/python-ci-linux.yml; proof tests/test-reusable-linux-lane.sh.
mutation-family:linux-lane

mutation-family:lint-gates
mutation-family:ci-image-ref
mutation-family:consumer-inventory
# windows/scripts/patches/ffmpeg/makedef writes every FFmpeg DLL's EXPORTS list: an
# ordinary build input no slug owns. Proof: linux/scripts/tests/test-ffmpeg-makedef.sh.
mutation-family:ffmpeg-makedef
# linux/scripts/lib/compiler-llvm-tools.sh picks a build tree's own LLVM tools: a
# library no slug owns. Proof: linux/scripts/tests/test-compiler-llvm-tools.sh.
mutation-family:compiler-llvm-tools

# renovate-local.sh and the modules beside it are the family's dependency-upgrade
# tool -- an ordinary script no preflight slug owns, proved by three suites of
# its own that the script-tests slug runs. The fifteen ids here each neuter one
# mechanic of a REFUSAL or of the UNDO (the exit code, the signal traps SIGPIPE
# included, the duplicate-key raise, the dry-run prediction, the rollback on a
# raising audit, the restored mtime, the kept backup, the joined pip
# continuation, the gitlink snapshot, the single settle across both halves, the
# undo on a failed submodule update, the marker an untrappable kill leaves and
# the refusal that reads it, the mapping written beside the copies) and name the
# suite that must then go red.
# docs/dependency-updates.md#the-mechanics-of-a-refusal
mutation-family:renovate

# shared-config owns sync-shared-config.sh, which READS this manifest but never
# names it on the preflight command line - the hub uses --ignore, not a manifest,
# so the data file is exercised only by the test suite. The mutation is real and
# bites there; what is missing is an ownership edge the registry can see.
# Anchoring it on the script instead was tried and rejected: --check never reaches
# the mode validation, so that proof would have been vacuous.
mutation-id:shared-config.exact-mode-is-declared-in-the-manifest
mutation-family:native-gcc-san
mutation-family:wheels-source
mutation-family:hailo
